<h3>Why</h3>
<p>
Most opensource projects use cryptographic hashes to identify their source code
and build inputs. Not all of them use cryptographic signatures to ensure
authenticity and integrity.</p>
<p>As long as consensus exists that there's valid
signatures for a given artifact, the build inputs can be considered authentic
even in projects that don't consume code signatures, as long as their
inputs are pinned to the same cryptographic hashes.
